    nameAr: 'آدم',
    titleEn: 'The First Human & First Prophet',
    storyEn: `Hazrat Adam (AS) is the father of all humanity and the very first Prophet Allah ever sent to this Earth. His story begins not on Earth, but in the heavens, when Allah announced to the angels: "I am placing a vicegerent on Earth." The angels were puzzled — they knew that humans would cause mischief and shed blood. But Allah told them: "I know what you do not know."

Allah created Adam (AS) from clay — He shaped his form from the soil of the Earth and then breathed His divine spirit into him. The moment that spirit entered Adam's body, he sneezed and said "Alhamdulillah" — Praise be to Allah — and Allah replied "Your Lord has mercy upon you." Adam was given something miraculous: Allah taught him the names of all things — every object, animal, concept, and creation. This was knowledge that even the angels did not possess.

To honour Adam, Allah commanded all the angels to prostrate before him as a sign of respect. Every angel obeyed — except Iblis (Shaytan), a jinn who had lived among the angels and had become arrogant. Iblis refused and said: "I am better than him — You created me from fire and created him from clay." This moment of pride and disobedience caused Iblis to be cursed and expelled from the heavens.

Allah placed Adam (AS) in the beautiful Garden of Paradise (Jannah) along with his wife Hawa (Eve), whom He created from Adam's own being to be his companion and comfort. They were given complete freedom to enjoy everything in Jannah — except one tree, which Allah forbade them from approaching.

Iblis, now filled with hatred and a desire for revenge, approached Adam and Hawa with whispers and deception. He swore by Allah that he was giving them sincere advice — that eating from the tree would make them angels or grant them eternal life. Our Lord, we have wronged ourselves, and if You do not forgive us and have mercy upon us, we will surely be among the losers — this was the sincere repentance Adam and Hawa made after they realised their mistake. Overwhelmed with shame, they covered themselves with leaves from Jannah and wept deeply. Allah in His boundless mercy accepted their repentance, but also decreed that they would now live on Earth as His representatives.

Adam and Hawa were sent down to Earth separately and were reunited at Mount Arafat near Makkah. Adam (AS) began his mission as the first Prophet: teaching his children and descendants to worship Allah alone, to pray, and to live righteously. He worked the land, built shelter, and established the foundations of human civilisation. He also built the first house of worship — a structure at the location of what would later become the Kaaba in Makkah.

Adam (AS) had many children, and among his sons were Habil (Abel) and Qabil (Cain). Qabil, in a moment of jealousy, killed his own brother Habil — making it the first murder in human history. Adam grieved deeply for this loss.

Hazrat Adam (AS) lived for approximately 1000 years on Earth according to various narrations. He continued to guide his descendants toward the worship of Allah until the end of his life. He passed away leaving behind the greatest legacy — humanity itself and the first tradition of divine worship on Earth. He is buried, according to scholars, in the region of what is now known as Iraq, though Allah knows best.`,

    storyRomanHindi: `Hazrat Adam (AS) tamam insaniyat ke baap hain aur Allah ke pehle nabi hain. Allah ne unhe mitti se banaya, unme apni rooh phoonki, aur phir farishton ko hukum diya ke unhe sajda karein. Sab ne sajda kiya, lekin Iblis ne takabbur ki wajah se inkar kar diya aur lanat ka shikar hua.

Allah ne Adam aur Hawa ko jannat mein rakha. Unhe sab kuch khane ki ijazat thi, siwa ek darakht ke. Iblis ne unhe baha karke us darakht ka phal khilaya. Unhone galti ki, sharminda hue, aur Allah se sachchi tauba ki. Allah ne unhe muaf kiya lekin zameen par bhej diya.

Zameen par Adam (AS) ne apni zindagi ka aaghaz kiya. Unhone apne bacho ko Allah ki ibadat sikhaya, zameen par kasht ki aur insani tamaddun ki bunyaad rakhi. Unke do bete the — Habil aur Qabil. Qabil ne hasad mein Habil ko qatl kar diya — ye insani tarikh ka pehla qatl tha.

Hazrat Adam (AS) takreeban 1000 saal tak zinda rahe. Inhone apni puri zindagi Allah ki ibadat aur apni aulad ki hidayat mein guzari. Aakhirkar jab unka waqt aaya, woh dunya se rukhsat ho gaye, apni naslon ko Allah ki rah par chod kar.`,

    storyRomanTelugu: `Hazrat Adam (AS) sampurna manavjati yokka taatayya mariyu Allah pampina modati Nabi. Allah aayananu matti nundi nirminchi, tana aatmanu oodaru, mariyu devaduutulanu aayanaku namaskaaram cheyyamandaru. Andaru namaskaaram chesaru — kaani Iblis, garvamulooni nishedhinchadu, mariyu shaapagrastu ayyadu.

Allah Adam mariyu Hawa nu Jannatlō nuncharu. Vaari kosam anni anumathimcharu — okka chettunu teesi. Iblis vaarini mosam chesi aa chettunu tinipinchadu. Varu tappu chesi, pashchaattapam tho Allah ni vesukunnaru. Allah vaarini kshaminchadu kaani bhoomiki pampu charu.

Bhoomipai Hazrat Adam (AS) tana jeevitam praarambhincharu. Tana pillalaku Allah ni pujinchaadam nerpistu, bhoomini sagubhadi chesi, maanava nagarikatha yokka paadhasiimaanu veesaru. Aayana rendu kodukulu unnaru — Habil mariyu Qabil. Qabil aasooyu tho Habil ni champadu — idi maanava charitra lō modati hatya.

Hazrat Adam (AS) daadu 1000 samvatsaralu jiivinchaaru. Tana sampurna jeevitaanni Allah seva mariyu tana santatini margadarshisataniki arpincharu.`,

