    id: 'shuaib',
    nameEn: 'Shuaib',
    nameAr: 'شعيب',
    titleEn: 'The Eloquent Prophet — Messenger to Midian',
    storyEn: `Hazrat Shuaib (AS) is described in Islamic tradition as one of the most eloquent and persuasive of all the Prophets — he was known for speaking with such clarity, wisdom, and beauty that he was called "the Khatib (Orator) of the Prophets." He is mentioned in the Quran multiple times and is connected to the story of two peoples: the Midianites and the People of the Forest (Ashab al-Aykah).

Midian was an ancient city and trading community in northwestern Arabia, near the Gulf of Aqaba, in a region that spans present-day Saudi Arabia, Jordan, and Sinai. The people of Midian were wealthy merchants and traders — but they had fallen into a serious moral and spiritual corruption. They had abandoned the worship of Allah and turned to idol worship. More importantly, they were notorious for dishonesty in trade: they gave short measure when selling, overcharged buyers, and used fraudulent weights and scales to cheat people.

Hazrat Shuaib (AS) was one of their own people. He rose among them as a Prophet and called them with both gentle persuasion and firm warning. His words are recorded beautifully in the Quran: "O my people, worship Allah — you have no deity other than Him. And do not give short measure or weight. Indeed, I see you in prosperity, but I fear for you the punishment of an all-encompassing Day."

He continued: "O my people, give full measure and weight in justice. Do not deprive people of their due, and do not commit abuse on Earth, spreading corruption." He urged them to see that honesty in trade was not just an ethical good — it was a fundamental act of worship, a demonstration of the fear of Allah in every business transaction.

The people of Midian responded with contempt and arrogance. They said: "O Shuaib, does your prayer command you that we should leave what our fathers worshipped? Indeed, we are in doubt about what you're saying." Their leaders threatened: "We will surely evict you from our city, O Shuaib, unless you return to our religion." Shuaib replied calmly: "Even if we are unwilling? We would be inventing a lie against Allah if we returned to your religion after Allah has rescued us from it."

He continued calling them for years, and the believers gathered around him. But the majority refused. Then the punishment came. Unlike the Aad (who were destroyed by a howling wind) and Thamud (who were destroyed by a thunderclap), the people of Midian were destroyed by what the Quran calls the Day of the Shadow (Yawm al-Zulla) — a searing, scorching heat followed by a dark cloud that then unleashed devastating fire upon them. The people of Aykah (a nearby forest community he also preached to) were destroyed similarly by a fire from the sky.

The believers with Shuaib (AS) were saved. He turned to the ruins of the city and said: "O my people, I have conveyed to you the messages of my Lord and I have given you sincere advice. How would I grieve for a disbelieving people?"

It is also worth noting that many Islamic scholars identify the "old righteous man" who employed Musa (AS) in Madyan as Hazrat Shuaib himself. If this is correct, then Shuaib (AS) also played a direct role in the life of Hazrat Musa — for Musa worked for him, married his daughter, and was shaped by his mentorship before receiving prophethood.

Hazrat Shuaib (AS) continued to live after the destruction of Midian, worshipping Allah and teaching the believers, and eventually passed away having fulfilled his mission.`,

    storyRomanHindi: `Hazrat Shuaib (AS) ko "Anbiya ke Khatib" — nabiyon ka khatiB — kaha jata tha, kyunki woh bahut khoobsurati se baat karte the. Quran mein kai jagah unka zikar hai. Woh Midian ke logon ke paas bheje gaye — ek taqatwar tijaarati qoam, jo hisaab mein kaami karte the aur logo ko thagti thi.

Hazrat Shuaib (AS) ne unhe pyaar aur hikmat se dakaar diya: "Meri qaum, sirf Allah ki ibadat karo aur tijaaratmein poora tol aur naap do. Allah ki saza se daro." Unhone kaha ke iman wali tijaarati Allah ki ibadat ka ek hissa hai.

Logon ne jawab diya: "Kya teri namaz tujhe kehti hai ke hum apne baap dada ka deen chhod dein?" Unhone dhamkiya di ke Shuaib ko shehar se nikaalen ge. Shuaib ne kaha: "Hum jhoot bol ke wapas nahi aa sakte."

Azab aaya — pehle jhalas-jhalaati garmi, phir andhere badal, phir aag. Midian waaloon ka khatma ho gaya. Shuaib (AS) aur imaan wale bachaye gaye. Kai ulema ye bhi mante hain ke Shuaib hi woh boodha naik insaan the jinhone Musa (AS) ko Madyan mein kaam par rakha tha.`,

    storyRomanTelugu: `Hazrat Shuaib (AS) ni "Nabiula Khatib" annaru — eendukante aayana chala akarpooramu tho matlaaduthaaru. Quranlo anekasaarlu aayana goorichi vassundhi. Aayana Midian prajalaku pampu chesar — oka balavantu vyaapaara samudaayam, vaarante vyapaaram lo mekkupovu chesevaru mariyu prajalanu mosagiinchevaru.

Hazrat Shuaib (AS) vaarini prema mariyu buddhi tho pilachinaadu: "Naa prajalaaraa, Allah ne matrame puujinchandi mariyu vyaparamlō poota kapi mariyu toolanni ivvanḍi. Allah yokka shaaxani bhayapadani." Aayana cheppinchadu ke neetimanthamayina vyaapaaram Allah yokka seva yokka oka bhaagam.

Prajalu samedhaanamichi: "Nee namaz maa poorvikula dharmaanni vadilandhaa?" Vaaru Shuaib ni nagaram nundi gummaka padathaamu ni abalaanu. Shuaib annaru: "Manam abaddhaalu cheppalemu."

Shiksha vacchindi — munda kasthungaa vedi, tarvata oka chhekata megham, tarvata agni. Midian nashanamayyindi. Shuaib (AS) mariyu nammakasthulu surakshitamgaa unnaru. Pala alimulu Musa (AS) ki Madyan lō pani ichchinaadi Shuaib ye annari.`,

    slides: [{"image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1509316785289-025f5b846b35?w=600&q=80","arabicText":"شعيب عليه السلام","captionEn":"Shuaib was sent to Madyan people who cheated in trade and gave less in weights and measures.","captionHindi":"Shuaib ko Madyan ke logon ki taraf bheja gaya jo tijaarat mein dhoka dete the.","captionTelugu":"Shuaib ni Madyan janaanike pathambaamu cheyyadam jarigindi vaallau vyaapaaram lo mosapu chesevaarau."},{"image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1537210249814-b9a10a161ae4?w=600&q=80","arabicText":"العدل","captionEn":"Shuaib called for justice and honesty. His people rejected him. Allah destroyed them with a thunderous blast.","captionHindi":"Shuaib ne insaaf aur imaandari ki dawat di. Qaum ne inkar kiya. Allah ne dahshataak awaz se tabah kiya.","captionTelugu":"Shuaib nyaayam mariyu niyaayaniki pilichaadu. Tiras karichaaru. Allah vaallanu gudugudumpu dhwanito nasanam cheshaadu."}],
